      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article describes 2 white male patients with probable splenic crisis caused by sickle cell trait after travel from sea level to a moderately high altitude. Both did well with return to lower altitude and conservative treatment. Although rare, this entity should be considered in patients presenting to the emergency department with left-sided chest or abdominal pain after travel to moderate or high altitude."},
